            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I doubt that the benchmark numbers that you present are meaningful. In the typed-list and local-swap cases, the C compiler can see through much of the code and should be able to move major parts of it out of the loop. It might even be able to discard the whole loop (or all but one iteration, depending on what `cy_pst` refers to) in the first case.",
