            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "\n\n> My feeling is that most of the obvious stuff is already done.\n\nI only suggest that it might be worth a quick check.\n\nIf there is nothing here, then oh well.\nThis isn't a problem to be solved, just thought it might have some benefit as a certain portion of the code might get a bit faster without explicit opt-in.\n\n> It might even be able to discard the whole loop (or all but one iteration, depending on what `cy_pst` refers to) in the first case.\n\nPy_ssize_t (fixed above). Hm, timings suggest that there was work done in the loop.\n\nSomething a bit less trivial.\n```python\ndef reverse(seq):\n    i: Py_ssize_t = 0\n    j: Py_ssize_t = len(seq)\n    rem: Py_ssize_t = j // 2\n    if not mode:\n        while rem:\n            rem -= 1\n\n            j -= 1\n            tmp = seq[j]\n            seq[j] = seq[i]\n            seq[i] = tmp\n            i += 1\n\n    elif mode == 1:\n        arr: list = seq\n        while rem:\n            rem -= 1\n\n            j -= 1\n            tmp = seq[j]\n            arr[j] = arr[i]\n            arr[i] = tmp\n            i += 1\n\n\nN = 100_000\nseq = list(range(N))\n%timeit this.reverse(seq)       # 1030\n%timeit this.reverse(seq, 1)    #  640\n```\n\n\n\n",
